course: dictionary
lesson: 5164
title: Irritate: annoy or sting
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Irritate» has two meanings. The first is to annoy someone or make them a bit angry, often by doing something again and again. The second is to make part of your body sore, itchy or red.
explain: «Smoke irritates the airways», so homes and cars should be smoke-free. The word tells you that smoke does something unpleasant to the inside of your body, not that it makes anyone cross.
explain: Read the words around the word to find its meaning. «A sneeze is a reflex that blasts air out of the nose and mouth to clear something irritating, like dust or pepper.» Dust and pepper make your nose tickle and sore, so irritating means something that causes that feeling.
fact: To irritate someone means to annoy them or make them a bit angry.
fact: To irritate skin or eyes means to make them sore, itchy or red.
fact: «Smoke irritates the airways», so it is not good for your breathing.
fact: «Toothpaste can irritate skin», so doctors don't recommend it for spots.
fact: Common phrases include «it irritates me when…», «get irritated» and «irritating habit».
exercise: «Smoke irritates the airways.» What does irritates mean here? | *Makes something sore and uncomfortable, in the body | Makes something sore and uncomfortable | Makes something shine brightly | Makes something very cold
exercise: Your little brother hums the same tune again and again. What does he do to you? | He helps you sleep | He makes you laugh | *He irritates you | He soothes you
exercise: Why do people wear gloves or goggles near some chemicals? | *To stop the chemicals irritating their skin or eyes | To make their hands glow | To keep their hands warm | To make the chemicals smell nicer
test: Which is the best example of an irritating habit? | Smiling at a friend | Reading a book quietly | *Humming the same tune over and over | Drawing a rainbow
test: Which of these is most likely to irritate your eyes? | Warm blanket | Soft music | *Smoke | Fresh sea breeze
exam: «A sneeze clears something irritating, like dust or pepper.» What is the best meaning of irritating here? | Bright and shiny | Sweet and sugary | Very heavy | *Tickly and annoying to the nose
